// Test: stdlib/json/json_encode_any_embedded_collection
// Semantic: FUNC-BUILTIN — `json.encode(any data)` must correctly serialize
//   typed collections (`list<T>`, `pairs<K,V>`) that are embedded as field
//   values inside an `any` object literal. The collections must be normalized
//   into JSON-tree format at boxing time so the recursive stringify walks
//   them correctly.
// Regression: JSON-ENCODE-ANY-EMBEDDED-LIST-LOST (dashboard fp 06ad82a75ad3).
//   Before compiler 0.30.302 a list literal embedded in an Any object literal
//   was boxed with the raw Clean list pointer as the payload, but the
//   stringify path expected the JSON-array layout (boxed Any per element).
//   The result was `{"items":[]}` for `any data = { items: [...] }`.
// Coupled fixes shipped together (each its own dashboard report):
//   - Typechecker's `infer_literal_expression` now recurses into nested
//     `Value::List` and produces a proper `ArrayLiteral` TAST node rather
//     than collapsing to `Literal(Null)`.
//   - `emit_box_any` routes `Array<T>` and `Pairs<K,V>` sources through
//     `__json_from_cln_list` / `__json_from_cln_pairs` stdlib helpers that
//     materialize the JSON-tree layout with each element re-boxed as Any.
//   - `wasmtime_runner`'s host `mem_alloc` now reads `__heap_ptr` at the
//     start so its `NEXT_ALLOCATION_OFFSET` cannot lag behind WASM-side
//     malloc and overwrite previously WASM-allocated regions.
//
// Expected output:
//   {"items":["a","b","c"]}
//   {"counts":[1,2,3],"name":"test"}
//   {"flags":[true,false,true]}
//   {"scores":[1.5,2.5,3.5]}

start:
	any d1 = { items: ["a", "b", "c"] }
	print(json.encode(d1))
	any d2 = { counts: [1, 2, 3], name: "test" }
	print(json.encode(d2))
	any d3 = { flags: [true, false, true] }
	print(json.encode(d3))
	any d4 = { scores: [1.5, 2.5, 3.5] }
	print(json.encode(d4))
